Custom topologies
=================

Put your own topology files in this directory. There are two ways to
describe one:

1. A lab configuration file (YAML, JSON, Python, C, C++, C#, Java,
   Ruby or COBOL) - no Mininet programming needed:

     mn-config validate custom/topo-2sw-2host.yaml
     sudo mn-config run custom/topo-2sw-2host.yaml

   or edit and run it in the browser:

     sudo mn-gui --config custom/topo-2sw-2host.yaml

   Start a new one with `mn-config init --lang yaml -o custom/mylab.yaml`.
   See docs/configuration.md.

2. A Python Topo class, loaded with `mn --custom`:

     sudo mn --custom custom/topo-2sw-2host.py --topo mytopo

   The file defines a `topos` dictionary mapping names to topology
   constructors, so you can then use the Mininet CLI or tests with it:

     sudo mn --custom custom/topo-2sw-2host.py --topo mytopo --test pingall

Both files in this directory describe the same network:

   h1 --- s3 --- s4 --- h2
